  "results_summary": [
    "33 of 35 Table S1 models were testable (7493 finite stimulus-response pairs). 15 had at least one habituating pair; Z=18 had none. 22 models had a habituating share outside 1-50% (the 18 zeros plus BIOMD0000000002, BIOMD0000000203, BIOMD0000000204 and BIOMD0000000600, each under 1%).",
    "Engagement passed: 32 of 33 testable models had at least one pair whose first pulse changed the response by a factor of 1.5 or more. The pre-registered rule therefore refutes (Z>=4 and a majority outside the band).",
    "A successive half-drop (ratio 1/2), recorded and not used for the verdict, occurred in 259 of 7493 finite pairs and in 11 models.",
    "Not testable, and not counted as failures: BIOMD0000000024 (delay() in the Octave export) and BIOMD0000000539 (reaction_production_A is referenced but never defined)."
  ],
  "deviations": [
    {
      "date": "2026-11-01",
      "what": "Each Table S1 model was integrated from its public BioModels Octave export, not by loading the SBML into a separate simulator.",
      "why": "Section 4.1 says the authors solved the Octave file after a small conversion to MATLAB. That export is the ODE they integrated. The allowed libraries are numpy, scipy and requests, which do not include an SBML engine. Pass and fail thresholds were not changed."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-11-01",
      "what": "A right-hand-side evaluation cap of 8000 calls per epoch treats that epoch as non-finite.",
      "why": "LSODA can stall on a bad Jacobian (observed on BIOMD0000000005). Pairs that do not finish are already outside the pre-registered finite-pair denominator. The habituation inequality was not changed. With the cap, BIOMD0000000005 finished with 128 of 144 pairs finite."
    }
  ]
